{"pagination":{"maxPageableSet":"10000","numFound":1,"query":"name=Bjarnason&limit=10&title=How Iceland Changed the World","limit":10,"start":0},"items":{"mods":{"titleInfo":[{"title":"How Iceland changed the world","subTitle":"the big history of a small island"},{"@type":"alternative","title":"Big history of a small island"}],"name":{"@nameTitleGroup":"1","@usage":"primary","@type":"personal","namePart":"Egill Bjarnason","role":[{"roleTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"creator"}},{"roleTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"author."}}]},"typeOfResource":"text","genre":[{"@authority":"marcgt","#text":"biography"},{"@authority":"rdacontent","#text":"text"},{"@authority":"aat","#text":"chronicles."},{"@authority":"fast","#text":"Annals and chronicles"},{"@authority":"fast","#text":"History"},{"@authority":"lcgft","#text":"Annals and chronicles"},{"@authority":"rvmgf","#text":"Annales et chroniques."}],"originInfo":[{"place":{"placeTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"nyu"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"New York (State)"}]},"dateIssued":{"@encoding":"marc","#text":"2021"},"issuance":"monographic"},{"@eventType":"publication","place":{"placeTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"[New York] :"}},"publisher":"Penguin Books,","dateIssued":[2021]}],"language":{"languageTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"eng"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"English"}]},"physicalDescription":{"form":[{"@authority":"marcform","#text":"print"},{"@type":"media","@authority":"rdamedia","#text":"unmediated"},{"@type":"carrier","@authority":"rdacarrier","#text":"volume"}],"extent":"xx, 266 pages ; 20 cm"},"abstract":{"@type":"Summary","#text":"\"The untold story of how one tiny island in the middle of the Atlantic has shaped the world for centuries. The history of Iceland began 1,200 years ago, when a frustrated Viking captain and his useless navigator ran aground in the middle of the North Atlantic. Suddenly, the island was no longer just a layover for the Arctic tern. Instead, it became a nation whose diplomats and musicians, sailors and soldiers, volcanoes and flowers, quietly altered the globe forever. How Iceland Changed the World takes readers on a tour of history, showing them how Iceland played a pivotal role in events as diverse as the French Revolution, the Moon Landing, and the foundation of Israel. Again and again, one humble nation has found itself at the frontline of historic events, shaping the world as we know it, How Iceland Changed the World paints a lively picture of just it all happened\"--"},"tableOfContents":"The discovery of the West -- The medieval legacy -- Iceland triggers a climate crisis -- Nationalism -- World War II -- The birth of Israel -- The moon landing -- The Cold War -- Gender equality.","note":[{"@type":"statement of responsibility","#text":"Egill Bjarnason."},"Includes index.",{"@type":"bibliography","#text":"Includes index."}],"subject":[{"geographicCode":{"@authority":"marcgac","#text":"e-ic---"}},{"@authority":"fast","topic":"Civilization"},{"@authority":"lcsh","geographic":"Iceland","topic":"History"},{"@authority":"lcsh","geographic":"Iceland","topic":"Civilization"},{"@authority":"rvm","geographic":"Islande","topic":"Histoire"},{"@authority":"fast","geographic":"Iceland"}],"classification":[{"@authority":"lcc","#text":"DL338 .E28 2021"},{"@edition":"23","@authority":"ddc","#text":"949.12"}],"relatedItem":[{"@type":"otherFormat","@otherType":"Online version:","@displayLabel":"Online version:","titleInfo":{"title":"How Iceland changed the world"},"name":{"namePart":"Egill Bjarnason."},"originInfo":{"publisher":"[New York] : Penguin Books, [2021]"},"identifier":{"@type":"local","#text":"(OCoLC)1249470713"}},{"@otherType":"HOLLIS record","location":{"url":"https://id.lib.harvard.edu/alma/99155660307903941/catalog"}}],"identifier":[{"@type":"isbn","#text":"9780143135883"},{"@type":"isbn","#text":"0143135880"},{"@type":"isbn","@invalid":"yes","#text":"97805